# Getting Started

## Installation

[% if ships_package %]
Add [[ project_name ]] to a project:

```console
uv add [[ project_name ]]
```

Or work on it from a checkout:
[% else %]
From a checkout:
[% endif %]

```console
uv sync
```
[% if ships_image %]

## Configuration

[[ project_name ]] runs with sensible defaults. To change them, set environment variables with the
`[[ python_package_name | upper ]]_` prefix, or put them in a `.env` file:

```console
export [[ python_package_name | upper ]]_ENVIRONMENT=production
export [[ python_package_name | upper ]]_DEBUG=true
```

See `Settings` in the {ref}`api-reference` for every option.

## Running

```console
uv run [[ project_name ]] --help
uv run [[ project_name ]] run
```

Or in docker, built from this checkout:

```console
docker compose -f docker/compose.yaml -f docker/compose.dev.yaml up --build
```
[% elif has_package %]

## Using it

```python
import [[ python_package_name ]]
```

See the {ref}`api-reference`.
[% endif %]
